] [17592186500034 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "b9e27368-2343-5732-958d-8a429ac47df7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500087 #edb/ref 1080 "-6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500087 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500087 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "d3062eb8-1be4-55c1-abe5-0531007f28e9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500147 #edb/ref 1080 "5(t+4)(t-1)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500147 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500147 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "ef378e59-9ad9-542b-aa16-7399d5fbff76" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500181 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186499830 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500181 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186499894 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500181 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186499956 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500181 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186499984 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500181 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186500087 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500181 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500181 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500181 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186499894 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500181 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "06764b2b-0fcb-5201-9043-354b15b5afa9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500206 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186499659 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500206 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186499886 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500206 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186499957 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500206 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186500003 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500206 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186500025 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500206 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500206 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500206 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186499659 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500206 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "37ecc6ff-8871-56b2-aab9-81dfb39a048c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500238 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186499791 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500238 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186499811 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500238 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186499955 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500238 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186500034 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500238 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186500147 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500238 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500238 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500238 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186499955 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500238 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "94c06265-2366-51a7-b0d0-03e55f741385" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500312 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186500238 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500312 #edb/ref 1069 "q-2855" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500312 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500312 #edb/ref 1071 "$5{t}^{2}-15t-20=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500312 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "51a9e6b4-a8d3-5a57-a795-b4c3e7575128" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500312 #edb/ref 1074 "First, notice that we can factor out $5$ from each of the terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5{t}^{2}-15t-20 & =5({t}^{2}-3t-4)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we just need to factor the polynomial ${t}^{2}-3t-4$ in parentheses.\n\nFirst, we find the factor pairs of the constant term $(-4).$ The constant term is negative, so that means one of the factors is negative and the other is positive:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & \\times (-4) \\\\ (-1) & \\times 4 \\\\ 2 & \\times (-2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find which factor pair adds up to the coefficient of the linear term $(-3):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1+(-4) & =-3 & ✓ \\\\ (-1)+4 & =3 & \\times  \\\\ 2+(-2) & =0 & \\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the factor pair identified above, we write the linear term as $-3t=t-4t$ and then factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2}-3t-4 & = \\\\ {t}^{2}+t-4t-4 & = \\\\ ({t}^{2}+t)+(-4t-4) & = \\\\ t(t+1)-4(t+1) & = \\\\ (t-4)(t+1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our original expression factors as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5({t}^{2}-3t-4) & =5(t-4)(t+1)\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500320 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186500181 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500320 #edb/ref 1069 "q-32107" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500320 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500320 #edb/ref 1071 "If $5{b}^{2}-15b+10=5(b+p)(b+q),$ then $p+q=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500320 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "7598e646-e70e-5042-8a78-36ec6c081791" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500320 #edb/ref 1074 "First, notice that we can factor out $5$ from each of the terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5{b}^{2}-15b+10 & =5({b}^{2}-3b+2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we just need to factor the polynomial ${b}^{2}-3b+2$ in parentheses.\n\nWe start by listing the factor pairs of the constant term $(2).$ We will want to find the factor pair that also adds up to the coefficient of the linear term $(-3),$ so we will consider the negative factor pairs in particular:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-1) & \\times (-2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find which factor pair adds up to the coefficient of the linear term $(-3):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-1)+(-2) & =-3 & ✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the factor pair identified above, we write the linear term as $-3b=-b-2b$ and then factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}^{2}-3b+2 & = \\\\ {b}^{2}-b-2b+2 & = \\\\ ({b}^{2}-b)+(-2b+2) & = \\\\ b(b-1)-2(b-1) & = \\\\ (b-2)(b-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our original expression factors as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5({b}^{2}-3b+2) & =5(b-2)(b-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $p=-2,q=-1,$ and $p+q=-3.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500345 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186500206 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500345 #edb/ref 1069 "q-80173" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500345 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500345 #edb/ref 1071 "Factor $6-3x-3{x}^{2}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500345 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b8115771-d0c0-58ad-81dd-b9545f4b8d28" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500345 #edb/ref 1074 "First, notice that we can factor out a $(-3)$ from each of the terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6-3x-3{x}^{2} & =-3({x}^{2}+x-2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we just need to factor the polynomial ${x}^{2}+x-2$ in parentheses.\n\nWe start by listing the factor pairs of the constant term $(-2).$ The constant term is negative, so that means one of the factors is negative and the other is positive:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & \\times (-2) \\\\ (-1) & \\times 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find which factor pair adds up to the coefficient of the linear term $(1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1+(-2) & =-1 & \\times  \\\\ (-1)+(2) & =1 & ✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nUsing the factor pair identified above, we write the linear term as $x=-x+2x$ and then factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3({x}^{2}+x-2) & = \\\\ -3({x}^{2}-x+2x-2) & = \\\\ -3(({x}^{2}-x)+(2x-2)) & = \\\\ -3(x(x-1)+2(x-1)) & = \\\\ -3(x+2)(x-1) & \\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
